<h2 class="text-secondary">Reconciliation Commission</h2><hr/>
<% id = modal('Functions of Reconciliation Commission', size: :lg) do %>
  Examples of matters on which the Reconciliation Commission ought to render
  decisions include:
  <ol>
    <li>cases in which the consequences or interpretation of a rule are
      uncertain.</li>
    <li>cases in which the application of a name is likely to endanger health
      or have serious economic consequences.</li>
    <li>cases where the application of a rule is likely to lead to
      confusion.</li>
    <li>proposals of neotype sequences (see SeqCode
      <%= link_to_rule('18c') %>).</li>
    <li>situations where the priority of names is unclear (see also SeqCode
      <%= link_to_rule('23c') %>).</li>
    <li>consideration of names proposed to be contrary to the General
      Considerations or Principles of the SeqCode
      (<%= link_to_rule('45') %>).</li>
    <li>other matters referred to it by the administrative components of the
      SeqCode Committee.</li>
  </ol>
<% end %>
<p class="lead">
  The Reconciliation Commission is the judicial branch of the SeqCode
  Committee and is the only body authorized to render decisions on the
  application of the SeqCode.
  <%= modal_button(id, class: 'text-primary') do %>
    Functions of the Reconciliation Commission
  <% end %>.
</p>
